-r / -R (Recursive): Deletes directories and all nested contents.

-f (Force): Suppresses confirmation prompts and ignores nonexistent files without throwing an error (e.g., rm -rf test_dir).

-i (Interactive / Safe Mode): Prompts for confirmation before deleting each file. Recommended for beginners:

Bash
rm -i note
# rm: remove regular empty file 'note'? y
Critical Safety Warning: The Dangerous rm -rf /
Because rm -rf deletes recursively and ignores all safety prompts without asking questions, running commands like sudo rm -rf / or typing a misplaced space like rm -rf / tmp/test will systematically erase the entire operating system root drive. Always double-check your path before pressing Enter.
